⚠️ **IMPORTANT: pin the new cleanup in the lane-guard suite (repo's own workflow-shape pattern)**

These two lines are load-bearing: without them the config-only pass re-adopts SPM residue on the persistent runner and the min-platform gate re-fires after a 10-50-minute SPM pass (run 39991663029: 1095.4s) — exactly the expensive feedback loop the gh-180 gate was built to avoid. Yet they are the only part of the gh-180 lane that nothing pins: the workflow's own env-block comment cites *"pinned by test/build_macos_spm_lane_guard_test.dart + test/macos_min_platform_gate_test.dart"*, and that suite's header calls this the *"workflow-shape test never-again"* pattern — but its AC2 currently only asserts `--config-only` + gate ordering, so a future refactor can silently drop the cleanup and the regression would only surface as a red deploy run on the runner.

Suggested extension (~10 lines) to AC2 in `test/build_macos_spm_lane_guard_test.dart`:

```dart
final cleanIdx = script.indexOf('flutter clean');
final rmIdx = script.indexOf("rm -rf macos/Flutter/ephemeral");
final configIdx = script.indexOf('flutter build macos --config-only');
expect(cleanIdx, greaterThan(-1),
    reason: 'gh-1800: SPM residue from pre-pin builds must be cleaned '
        'before the config pass or the gate re-fires after a 1000s+ pass');
expect(rmIdx, greaterThan(-1));
expect(cleanIdx, lessThan(configIdx), reason: 'clean must precede config-only');
```

(Adjust the asserted `rm` paths to whatever survives the comment3 discussion — pin what actually ships.)

